// Commutative + associative `+`. These are exactly the rewrites that produce
// "the same pattern with its variables reordered" — the blow-up the slotted
// seen-set is meant to fold. comm is pure variable reordering (handled natively
// by alpha-equivalence in the slotted seen-egraph); assoc reshapes the tree
// (handled by DSR saturation).
comm:  (+ ?a ?b) <=> (+ ?b ?a)
assoc: (+ (+ ?a ?b) ?c) <=> (+ ?a (+ ?b ?c))
